strings.SAM_web_of_tensions_category_desc:
As the state expands, General Artsezo and his supporters must constitute individual regional authorities, through appointing governors from his own inner circle, other military cliques, or general civilian functionaries.

All three factions exist in an uneasy equilibrium, and balance must be maintained between their appointments if order is to be maintained and state unrest prevented.

